# Constitution

Reviewer-facing projection of `AGENTS.md` in `{{control_repo}}` and the
product repositories' code-review focus. Applies to every repository of the
`{{org}}` project on {{board_url}}:

{{repos}}

`AGENTS.md` is canonical; amend this projection alongside invariant changes.

## Core principles

### I. Architecture invariants
`{{source_of_truth}}` owns the architecture. These invariants hold in every
change; breaking one is a blocking finding unless a dated decision records
why it changes:

{{invariants}}

### II. Credentials and secrets
No secret, token or authenticated URL reaches source, logs, pull request
bodies, issues or prompts. Credentials stay with the system that owns them and
are never copied, printed or widened to make progress.

### III. Specified, story-scoped work
Every change implements one pinned user story or one issue's acceptance
criteria. A change outside that scope is a new story. A spec change is a new
commit in the control repository and a re-pinned issue.

### IV. Tested behaviour
Every story has testable acceptance scenarios and named tests. Tests cover
failure and edge paths, not only the happy path, and run against disposable
resources, never production.

### V. Recorded decisions
Non-trivial decisions are recorded with date, rationale and rejected
alternative in the control repository, never in a product repository.

## Code review focus

{{review_focus}}

## Quality and workflow

Use the pinned spec, plan, tasks and this constitution for the assigned story;
otherwise use the issue's acceptance criteria. Complete code, tests and
self-review fixes before running tests. Run every gate in the affected
repository's `AGENTS.md` once the work is ready and before a pull request is
opened or repaired. UI changes include desktop and mobile visual verification.

Autop owns board status and scheduling. One pull request per affected
repository; epic sub-PRs branch from and target the recorded integration
branch. Review findings are BLOCKING / SHOULD / NIT; approval means no
blockers remain. Agents do not merge or change routing policy.

## Governance

Amend this constitution together with the playbook change that motivates it,
and verify it in review.

